psql-manager keeps ~/.pg_service.conf and ~/.pgpass in sync, one service at a time.

Usage: psql-manager <command> [arguments]
       psql-manager              (on a terminal: pick a service in the TUI and connect)

Commands:
  add      add a service to both files
  list     list services
  show     show one service in detail
  edit     change a service; .pgpass follows host/port/dbname/user
  rm       remove a service and its managed .pgpass entry
  search   search name, desc, tags, host and dbname
  connect  connect with psql (pick in the TUI without a name)
  test     check that psql can connect (select 1)
  doctor   check both files for problems
  path     print the files and psql in use

Environment:
  PGSERVICEFILE      service file (default ~/.pg_service.conf)
  PGPASSFILE         password file (default ~/.pgpass)
  PSQL_MANAGER_PSQL  psql to run (default: psql in PATH)
  XDG_STATE_HOME     connection history goes to $XDG_STATE_HOME/psql-manager/history
                     (default ~/.local/state/psql-manager/history)

Exit codes:
  0 success, 2 usage error, 3 service not found, 4 file or permission error,
  5 connection failed

Run 'psql-manager help <command>' for details.
